desc:GFX G RS50 [drum machine]
//tags: instrument drum machine rhythm digital 505 sequencer lo-fi stereo
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-thick, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-dyn (.jsfx-inc) in the same
// folder.
//
// RS50 - the RS series' little stereo machine, in the spirit of the mid-80s budget rhythm composer with sixteen
// sounds and a stereo mix. No samples: every sound is synthesised when the plug-in loads ("baked") at the original's
// 25 kHz clock and stored as plain 8-bit (the cymbals 6-bit): a hard, clicky kick, dark ringing toms, slapping congas
// and clanging cowbells built from their bodies' resonances. As on the original, related sounds share a voice, so each
// cuts the other off: the hats, the two congas, the toms and timbale, the two cowbells, clap and rim, crash and ride.
//
// VOICES (sixteen channels, each with LEVEL and PAN): BASS, SNARE, LO / MID / HI TOM, RIM, CLAP, CLOSED HAT, OPEN HAT
// (CH cuts off a ringing OH), CRASH, RIDE, LO / HI CONGA, TIMBALE, LO / HI COWBELL ("BELL").
//   ACCENT: how far apart accents and plain hits are (plain hits sit back, accents jump out; 50 % = about 6 dB). The voices meet in a stereo mix bus with a soft analogue drive.
//
// SEQUENCER: 16 patterns of 16 steps per channel (off / hit / accent), LAST STEP per pattern, SWING. It never starts
//   running by itself: press RUN. While REAPER plays, it locks to the timeline (bar 1 = step 1); while REAPER is
//   stopped, RUN free-runs at the project tempo. A new pattern takes over at the end of the bar.
// MIDI: notes play the voices too (GM drum map: 35 / 36 BD, 38 / 40 SD, 41 LT, 45 MT, 48 HT, 37 RS, 39 CP, 42 CH,
//   46 OH, 49 CR, 51 RD, 64 LC, 63 HC, 65 / 66 TI, 68 LB, 56 HB); velocity above 100 = accent. MIDI passes through.
//
// FOLLOW: the sequencer starts and stops with REAPER's transport (off by default: it never starts by itself).
// PATTERNS: a bank of 15 patterns; a new instance starts with them in patterns 1 - 15 (PATTERN > Load a pattern from
//   the bank brings any of them back). PATTERN also clears or copies the pattern.
// EDIT (layer B): a TUNE (+/- 12 semitones) and an amp envelope - ATTACK, DECAY, SUSTAIN, RELEASE - for every
//   instrument. SUSTAIN holds for the gate (one step from the sequencer, the held note from MIDI); SUSTAIN 100 % with
//   RELEASE at NATURAL (the default) leaves the sound as it is. Presets reset layer B to its defaults.
//
// SIGNAL FLOW: the voices > PAN > the stereo mix bus (soft drive) > the FX strip, in this order: PHASER > DRIVE > COMP >
//   DELAY (each with its IN key) > THICK > LEVEL > the house output stage (CLIP, -0.3 dBFS).
//
// DRIFT (0 - 100 %, 50 % = standard): a cheap stereo mixer that never quite sits still.
//   drive      how hard the voices hit the mix bus wanders slowly (+/- 3 dB around its light standard drive), so the
//              grit breathes
//   pan        each voice's place in the stereo field wanders slowly around its PAN (+/- 15 %), and each hit lands a
//              little to one side (+/- 5 %)
//   0 % = none (fixed drive, fixed pans), 100 % = twice the standard amount, a little faster.
//
// PAD ORDER AND COLOURS: the voices are laid out BD, SN, RIM, CLAP, HH, OH, HT, MT, LT, RD, CR (then the percussion)
//   on the panel, the grid and the EDIT page, colour-coded by family (kick brown, snare / rim red, clap orange,
//   hats yellow, toms green, cymbals blue, percussion violet; darker = lower). The MIDI notes are unchanged.
// GUI: in the dress of the 34 series instruments (charcoal, sharp-cornered sections, knurled caps, lit keys). Click a
//   step to cycle off > hit > accent; drag to paint the same value along a row. Click a track name to hear it. Values show while a knob is touched.
// PRESETS (12): kits - levels, pans, swing and FX, level-matched to Init on a groove; they never change the patterns.
//   (Patterns: see PATTERNS above.)
// Latency: 0 samples.
//
// TWEAK points are marked TWEAK.
// STATUS: Stable v2.0 (from the Lab, Oct 2026). v0.7 (wider ACCENT; complete: sound engine, sequencer, FX strip, faceplate, presets).

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-thick.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-dyn.jsfx-inc

slider1:ac_lvl=50<0,100,1>-Accent (%)
slider2:lv_bd=80<0,100,1>-Bass level (%)
slider3:lv_sd=70<0,100,1>-Snare level (%)
